CORE
main.c
--dfcc main --apply-loop-contracts _ --signed-overflow-check --no-assertions
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
^\[main\.(loop_invariant_step\.)?\d+\] line 4 Check (invariant after step for loop main\.0|that loop invariant is preserved): FAILURE$
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
--
--
The check that the loop invariant is inductive (here it is not) is a check
of the loop's contract, not one of the user's assertions: --no-assertions
keeps it. (goto_convert marked it user-provided, and the invariant, which
the loop then assumed, made the overflow after the loop unreachable.)
